Fix compilation with libc++ (ROCM/clr part)

Regenerated from hip-6.3.0-clr-fix-libcxx.patch for ROCm 10.0, keeping only the
half that is still required.

The dropped half saved and restored the __local macro around the
<include/cuda_wrappers/*> includes, because libc++'s <queue> uses __local as an
identifier while HIP defined it as an address-space attribute. ROCm 10.0
removed `#define __local` from the tree entirely (device_library_decls.h no
longer defines it anywhere), so that workaround has nothing left to guard.

Still needed: <__clang_cuda_complex_builtins.h> refers to ::max, which arrives
via <__clang_hip_math.h>; upstream still does not include it first.
--- a/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_runtime.h
+++ b/hipamd/include/hip/amd_detail/amd_hip_runtime.h
@@ -394,6 +394,8 @@
 #pragma push_macro("__CUDA__")
 #define __CUDA__
 #include <__clang_cuda_math_forward_declares.h>
+// __clang_cuda_complex_builtins wants ::max
+#include <__clang_hip_math.h>
 #include <__clang_cuda_complex_builtins.h>
 // Workaround for using libc++ with HIP-Clang.
 // The following headers requires clang include path before standard C++ include path.
